\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs28\b Moen Smart Shower (U by Moen) - Standalone Driver\b0\fs22\par
\par
Unofficial / community driver. Not affiliated with or supported by Moen, Fortune Brands, or Control4.\par
\par
\b Overview\b0\par
This driver controls a Moen Smart Shower / U by Moen digital shower valve directly from the Control4 controller: it authenticates to Moen's cloud, polls status over REST, and sends on/off, temperature, outlet, and preset commands over Moen's real-time Pusher WebSocket channel. No external bridge machine is required for this version.\par
\par
\b Setup\b0\par
1. Add the driver to your project and bind it to a room.\par
2. In the driver's Properties, enter your U by Moen account email and password (the same account used by the Alexa/Android U by Moen app).\par
3. Leave "Device Serial Number Override" blank to auto-select the account's shower, or enter a specific serial if the account has more than one.\par
4. Confirm "Cloud Status" reads Authenticated and "Pusher Status" reads Connected / subscribed within about a minute.\par
5. Check "Outlet 1-4 Position" properties against the driver's Print Debug Info action output if your shower has a different outlet layout than positions 1-4.\par
\par
\b Proxies\b0\par
- Shower: main run/temperature control (light_v2). ON/OFF starts or stops the shower; the dimmer level maps to target temperature between the "Target Temp Min/Max (F)" properties.\par
- Shower - Outlet 1 through 4: individual outlet on/off (light_v2, no dimming). Mapped to real outlet "position" numbers via the Outlet N Position properties.\par
\par
\b Commands / Actions\b0\par
- Activate Preset (Position 1-4): activates a saved Moen shower preset.\par
- Resume Paused Shower: resumes water flow after a preset paused it at temperature.\par
- Refresh Status: polls Moen's cloud immediately instead of waiting for the next scheduled poll.\par
- Print Debug Info: dumps current state to the driver log.\par
\par
\b Support\b0\par
This is an unofficial community project. See the driver's Lua source header comments for the full technical rationale, confirmed API details, and known limitations.\par
